note S3 abstract: a constructor body that is not exactly the dup32 form keeps the runtime check;
note here the value breaks the invariant for every x, so the program traps 10 (exit 110)
om2
abstract dup32 ulong
holds dup32 dup32
fn dup32mk x uint to dup32
ret seal dup32 or shl ulong x 32 ulong add x 1
end
fn main to int
d = dup32mk 5
ret int and open d 1
end
